# FLAC -- the lossless codec, packaged for libsndfile rather than for itself.
#
# The chain this sits at the bottom of: gnome-settings-daemon hard-requires
# libpulse-mainloop-glib, pulseaudio's client library takes `sndfile` as a BARE
# dependency() that no option can drop, and libsndfile takes FLAC, Ogg, Vorbis
# and Opus as an all-or-nothing group. So a lossless audio codec is on the
# critical path to the desktop's settings daemon, which is not a sentence
# anybody would guess from the dependency page.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://github.com/xiph/flac/releases/download/1.5.0/flac-1.5.0.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=f2c1c76592a82ffff8413ba3c4a1299b6c7ab06c734dee03fd88630485c2b920
SRC_DIR=flac-1.5.0

# --enable-ogg IS THE LOAD-BEARING FLAG HERE, AND IT IS ALREADY THE DEFAULT.
# That combination is exactly the one this tree keeps getting caught by, so it
# is stated rather than assumed. configure.ac:339-346 reads:
#
#     AC_ARG_ENABLE([ogg], ..., [ want_ogg=$enableval ], [ want_ogg=yes ] )
#     if test "x$want_ogg" != "xno"; then
#         XIPH_PATH_OGG(have_ogg=yes,
#             AC_MSG_WARN([*** Ogg development environment not installed ...]))
#     fi
#
# A MISSING libogg IS A WARNING. Not an error, not a configure failure -- a
# warning in the middle of several hundred lines of configure output, after
# which have_ogg=no and the package builds, links, installs and passes every
# path check with Ogg-FLAC support silently absent. The flag cannot prevent
# that (it is already yes); only an assertion on the artefact can, and install.sh
# carries it.
#
# XIPH_PATH_OGG is a HAND-WRITTEN HEADER-AND-LIBRARY PROBE (m4/ogg.m4), not
# PKG_CHECK_MODULES -- it looks for ogg/ogg.h and -logg under a --with-ogg
# prefix. That is why this recipe declares no pkgconf build dependency where
# nearly every other one does: configure.ac contains no PKG_PROG_PKG_CONFIG and
# no PKG_CHECK_MODULES at all. The .pc file flac installs is produced by plain
# autoconf substitution, which needs no pkg-config to exist.
#
# --disable-cpplibs drops libFLAC++, the C++ binding. Nothing in this tree
# consumes it: libsndfile uses the C API, and it is the only consumer flac is
# here for. Stripping the package to the library it is packaged FOR is the gcr-3
# precedent, and install.sh asserts libFLAC++ ABSENT so the decision is held by
# the recipe rather than by whoever remembers it.
#
# --disable-doxygen-docs: the option defaults TRUE and then does
# AC_CHECK_PROGS(DOXYGEN, doxygen), which is a soft lookup -- so today it
# resolves to nothing because doxygen is not packaged, and it would start
# building API documentation on the first rebuild after anyone packages it.
# finish_install deletes /usr/share/doc regardless, so that would be build time
# spent on a directory this tree throws away.
#
# --disable-version-from-git: defaults yes and asks git for the version string.
# There is no .git in a release tarball so it falls back correctly today, but a
# build whose output depends on whether a VCS is present is a build that is a
# function of its environment rather than of this recipe.
#
# --disable-examples: built but not installed. Compile time for nothing.
#
# NOT PASSED, deliberately: --disable-thorough-tests, which BLFS uses. It only
# selects how much work `make check` does, and no recipe here runs the test
# suite; passing it would imply this build tests something.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--disable-static \
--enable-ogg \
--disable-cpplibs \
--disable-doxygen-docs \
--disable-version-from-git \
--disable-examples"
